Notebook[{
Cell["BlackBox: Contextuality Certificates", "Title",ExpressionUUID->"44f8b5df-36fb-6449-94c6-2d0673a1f211"],

Cell["\<\
Graph- and sheaf-theoretic certificates of quantum contextuality: three \
bounds (independence number, Lovasz theta, fractional packing), exclusivity \
filters under composition, the contextual fraction, Abramsky-Brandenburger \
local-global analysis, the \:010cech obstruction of the support presheaf, \
and the so(3) interface of the KCBS cascade. Load with \
Needs[\"HubertKolcz`BlackBox`\"].\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"ccab2f85-2a65-3541-827f-29cbe3448f2c"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["AvNArgument", "InlineCode"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "AvNArgument[scen, e] and AvNArgument[scen, e, d] give the All-vs-Nothing \
argument of the empirical model e on the scenario scen over Z_d (default d = \
2; d any integer >= 2, prime or composite), following \
Abramsky-Barbosa-Kishida-Lal-Mansfield, arXiv:1502."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"5c7d3f92-2e48-4b61-8a05-d94e17b26c38"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["CascadeGenerators", "InlineCode"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "CascadeGenerators[] gives the four so(3) generators (matrix logarithms of \
the stage-frame transition rotations) of the Lapkiewicz KCBS cascade."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"4cc01417-ab32-c845-a944-7c6ddf0fff72"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["CechCohomology", "InlineCode"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "CechCohomology[scen, e] gives the absolute \:010cech cohomology of the \
Z-linearized support presheaf of the empirical model e over the cover of \
scen: an association with \"H0Rank\" (rank of the module of compatible \
Z-linear families = global sections), \"H1FreeRank\" and \"H1Torsion\" \
(elementary divisors > 1 of the degree-0 coboundary, by Smith normal form), \
\"CochainRanks\", \"CoboundaryRanks\", \"ComplexCloses\", and \
\"SupportNoSignalling\"."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"9d4e2a86-1b73-4c25-8e60-f7a15b39c4d2"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["CechObstruction", "InlineCode"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "CechObstruction[scen, e] gives the \:010cech cohomological obstruction \
data of the support presheaf of the empirical model e on the scenario scen \
(Abramsky-Mansfield-Barbosa; Abramsky-Barbosa-Kishida-Lal-Mansfield, \
arXiv:1502."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"7f2a9c41-88d3-4b46-9a17-c3e5d20b6a94"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["CechRelativeCohomology", "InlineCode"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "CechRelativeCohomology[scen, e, c0] gives the RELATIVE \:010cech cohomology \
of the Z-linearized support presheaf of the empirical model e with respect \
to the distinguished context c0 (an index into scen[\"Contexts\"], or the \
context itself): the presheaf F~ = ker(F -> F|c0), whose value on U is \
spanned by differences of support sections agreeing on U \[Intersection] c0 \
(so F~(c0) = 0)."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"8b3f5a29-6d17-4e84-9c02-a4d7e58f1b63"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["CEFilter", "InlineCode"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "CEFilter[g, p] and CEFilter[g, p, k] apply the Consistent-Exclusivity \
filter at k copies (default 2) to the probability assignment p (a vector in \
VertexList order) on the exclusivity graph g: every maximal clique of the \
k-fold OR (conormal) power must carry total probability at most 1 under the \
factorization rule P(e1,."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"d2acfc61-322e-704c-a608-edc5c09dbda8"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["CEFilterMixed", "InlineCode"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "CEFilterMixed[{{g1, p1}, {g2, p2}, ...}] applies the Consistent-Exclusivity \
filter to the independent composition of DIFFERENT experiments: exclusivity \
graphs g_i with assignments p_i (vectors in VertexList order); joint events \
are exclusive iff exclusive in some factor and weights multiply."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"3a86d17f-92c4-4b5e-8d09-6ef42b71c5a8"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["ContextualFraction", "InlineCode"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "ContextualFraction[scen, e] gives CF = 1 - NoncontextualFraction[scen, e], \
the contextual resource content of the empirical model e."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"3279bef5-f9e8-f448-9952-2f35a4e8b5b2"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["CoverScenario", "InlineCode"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "CoverScenario[X, cover] gives the contextuality scenario of an arbitrary \
measurement cover as an association: measurements X, contexts = the elements \
of cover (ordered measurement lists), section order per context (Tuples of \
the outcome sets in context order), the Abramsky-Brandenburger incidence \
matrix \"Incidence\" relating deterministic global assignments to context \
sections, \"Assignments\" (all global assignments), and \"Outcomes\"."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"2b8e5d17-6c94-4f0a-b3d2-91a47e08c5f3"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["CycleCoboundary", "InlineCode"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "CycleCoboundary[n] gives the cellular-sheaf coboundary \[Delta] (2n x 4n) \
of the n-cycle cover with marginalization restriction maps (Hansen-Ghrist, \
arXiv:1808."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"3f9e0608-a6db-6d4a-a1c3-489055112d4a"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["CycleModel", "InlineCode"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "CycleModel[n, p00, p10] gives the symmetric empirical model vector on the \
n-cycle with edge distribution (p00, p10, p10, 0)."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"3398f17e-dc23-fa46-a7db-e07cbeab2c21"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["CycleORProduct", "InlineCode"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "CycleORProduct[{n1, n2, ...}] gives the OR (conormal) product of the \
cycles C_n1, C_n2, ... on explicit tuple vertices: joint events are exclusive \
iff exclusive in some factor."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"6e91b8a3-4f57-4a2c-b7d9-0c83e5f21d46"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["CycleScenario", "InlineCode"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "CycleScenario[n] gives the n-cycle contextuality scenario as an \
association: measurements 0."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"faeb794a-74e9-cb40-a116-eacd3c80efbf"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["DLADimension", "InlineCode"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "DLADimension[gens] gives the dimension of the dynamical Lie algebra \
generated by the antisymmetric matrices gens after one commutator step: the \
rank of the generator axes together with all pairwise commutator axes."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"d9eec872-325b-e249-82d6-44b53cf6967b"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["FractionalPackingNumber", "InlineCode"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "FractionalPackingNumber[g] gives the fractional packing number \[Alpha]*(g) \
as an exact linear program over the maximal cliques: the exclusivity-only \
(E-principle, single copy) bound."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"5d591db1-8137-1a48-924e-bfef61e6b200"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["GlobalSectionQ", "InlineCode"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "GlobalSectionQ[scen, e] gives True if the empirical model e extends to a \
global probability distribution (a nonnegative global section of the \
Abramsky-Brandenburger presheaf): the model is noncontextual."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"81155152-cd61-ad41-8228-86f9d8a7536a"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["GlueGraphs", "InlineCode"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "GlueGraphs[g, h, ident] glues graph h onto graph g identifying vertices by \
the rules ident: {hVertex -> gVertex, ."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"e2b54c49-0ee4-054c-9828-b158f9e8bfe6"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["HarmonicResidual", "InlineCode"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "HarmonicResidual[delta, e] gives Norm[delta ."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"0a59680e-a750-224e-a391-1ba710f0bc15"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["IndependenceNumber", "InlineCode"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "IndependenceNumber[g] gives the independence number \[Alpha](g): the \
noncontextual (deterministic hidden-variable) bound of the exclusivity graph \
g."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"fabb275a-1102-2646-ba1c-9b41724fc0eb"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["KCBSDirections", "InlineCode"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "KCBSDirections[] gives the five exact pentagram unit vectors of the KCBS \
construction (cyclically orthogonal, cone axis {0,0,1})."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"56bdd903-3721-0747-aee5-78eb16380241"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["LovaszTheta", "InlineCode"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "LovaszTheta[g] gives the Lov\[AAcute]sz number \[CurlyTheta](g) by \
semidefinite programming: the quantum bound of the exclusivity graph g (CSW, \
arXiv:1010."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"f643c152-d26b-ff43-91b1-7800efee2888"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["LovaszThetaSparse", "InlineCode"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "LovaszThetaSparse[g] gives the Lov\[AAcute]sz number \[CurlyTheta](g) by \
chordal decomposition of the dual semidefinite program: one small block per \
maximal clique of a chordal extension of g, so the cost scales with the \
treewidth of g instead of its vertex count."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"a91c3d47-5e28-4b06-8f13-27d90c65e4b2"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["NoncontextualFraction", "InlineCode"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "NoncontextualFraction[scen, e] gives the noncontextual fraction NCF of the \
empirical model e in the scenario scen (Abramsky-Barbosa-Mansfield, PRL 119, \
050504): the maximal total weight of a subprobability mixture of \
deterministic global assignments dominated by e."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"cc60eb11-a1e2-ec40-a842-44b16d02ac2d"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["PentagonChain", "InlineCode"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "PentagonChain[n] gives the chain of n single-edge-glued pentagons (3n+2 \
vertices): the mesh whose \[CurlyTheta] grows linearly while any state-vector \
treatment grows as 2^(5n)."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"0ac08b76-af91-8e47-a5c3-3f41558ff2ad"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["PentagonRing", "InlineCode"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "PentagonRing[n] gives the ring of n single-edge-glued pentagons (3n \
vertices, 4n edges)."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"84d2f6b1-9a35-4e08-bc47-1f60a72d93e5"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["PossibilisticSupport", "InlineCode"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "PossibilisticSupport[scen, e] gives the possibilistic global support S_e of \
the empirical model e: association with \"Size\" (number of global \
assignments consistent with the support of e) and \"Empty\" (True means \
strong contextuality, AB Sec."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"f34aa923-7e01-364f-8ad8-def3ae38ca72"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["QuantumEventProbability", "InlineCode"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "QuantumEventProbability[n] gives the per-event probability \
cos(Pi/n)/(1+cos(Pi/n)) of the quantum-maximal n-cycle model (Araujo et al., \
PRA 88, 022118); for n = 5 it is 1/Sqrt[5]."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"c58f0e27-6d43-49b2-9a81-e35d708c14b7"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["So3Axis", "InlineCode"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "So3Axis[m] gives the rotation-axis vector (vee map) of the antisymmetric \
3x3 matrix m."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"c7991bd3-1ebb-f346-975f-cde610374d68"]
},
FrontEndVersion->"15.0 for Microsoft Windows (64-bit) (May 19, 2026)",
